 Both inputs must be JSON values. Operations are evaluated in order and processing stops at the first
 RFC 6902 error; because the input document is never changed, a failed patch leaves it intact.
 
+`createPatch(from, to)` creates an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that changes `from` into `to`. It recursively
+targets changed object members and array elements, so a small change does not replace an entire
+document. Both inputs must be JSON values and remain unchanged.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+createPatch(
+  { user: { name: "Ada", theme: "light" } },
+  { user: { name: "Ada", theme: "dark" } },
+);
+// [{ op: "replace", path: "/user/theme", value: "dark" }]
+```
+
 ## JSON Merge Patch
 
 `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies an [RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
