@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+id: task-005-add-rfc-6902-patch-creation
+type: task
+title: "Add RFC 6902 patch creation"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Export `createPatch(from, to)` to generate an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that changes
+one JSON value into another without mutating either input.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Added `createPatch`, including JSON-value validation and cloned operation
+  values so the generated patch shares no mutable containers with its inputs.
+- Recursively diffed object members and array elements. Array alignment uses a
+  longest-common-subsequence scan to retain insertions and removals as local
+  operations; changed elements are recursively diffed where they align.
+- Escaped JSON Pointer reference tokens and documented the new public API.
+
+## Acceptance and verification
+
+All new behaviours were tested red-first: localized nested changes, array
+insertion and local array-element updates, pointer escaping, root replacement,
+input validation, and input independence. The first test run failed because
+`createPatch` was not exported. After implementation, `npm test` passed all 34
+tests; pairwise patch round-trip checks and `git diff --check` also passed.
